//! The `font-size-adjust` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property adjusts
//! the size of a font to match a chosen font metric, such as the height of lowercase letters, to a
//! specified proportion of the `font-size`. This property is intended for adjusting fallback fonts
//! to have similar metrics as the first-choice font.
//!
//! Initial: none. Inherited: yes.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - from-font: Uses the `<number>` value for the specified `<font-metric>` from the first available
//! font.
//! - none: No font size adjustment is applied.
//!
//! Grammar: none | [ ex-height | cap-height | ch-width | ic-width | ic-height ]? [ from-font |
//! <number [0,∞]> ]
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-fonts-5/#propdef-font-size-adjust
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-size-adjust
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

